#lang saffron
;; codegen-gcc14-permerrors, the Saffron container seam.
;;
;; The D5 boundary unboxes an `any` argument to the callee's parameter type.
;; That cast used to be spelled from the target's bare TypeKind alone
;; (`type_simple(kind)`), which for a heap ADT app collapses to the int64
;; carrier -- so the emitted C assigned an integer to a typed pointer:
;;
;;   tur_adt_Vec__any *__t0 = (int64_t)(intptr_t)TUR_UNTAG(__tur_c);
;;
;; `-Wint-conversion`. A warning through GCC 13, and a HARD ERROR from GCC 14
;; on, which is what makes it worth a fixture rather than a note: an
;; unannotated container parameter is the dialect's headline case, and it did
;; not build at all on a modern toolchain.
;;
;; THE ASSERTION IS NOT THE OUTPUT. `tests/run.sh` carries a ratchet that fails
;; any fixture whose emitted C produces -Wint-conversion or
;; -Wincompatible-pointer-types (see the block in run.sh, and
;; docs/archive/emitted-c-pointer-integer-warnings-unwatched.md). The ratchet
;; was already there and already correct -- what was missing was a fixture that
;; exercised this shape, so nothing ever handed it the warning.
;;
;; `vec-get` alone does NOT reproduce it (the existing
;; saffron-unannotated-container-param fixture passes without this fix); the
;; fold's callee is what takes the container by typed pointer. So the shape
;; here is specific, not incidental.
;;
;; Same class as the match-arm binder fix: a bare kind consulted at a site where
;; the full resolved type was in hand.

(defn total [v]
  (vec-fold v 0 (fn [acc x] (+ acc x))))

(defn total-f [v]
  (vec-fold v 0.0 (fn [acc x] (+ acc x))))

(defn main []
  (println (cast (total [1 2 3]) int))
  ;; a fractional float: an integral one could not show a truncation on the way
  ;; back through the carrier
  (println (cast (total-f [1.5 2.25 0.5]) float))
  0)
